& [VerbatimUserMessage] is the preserved user message
  + [text] is "Cantor needs to have a calendar and planner, and that planner will probably be central to it's operations. Oh, and I want to have it running with a \"repo\" that's taking snapshots of diffs at every moment, and applying the thoughtfulness patterns I described in the project Walking Attention where it gives attention to the change log of a repo commit, reflecting on what work had been done over the changes expressed in the diff log. this gives a backwards-reflecting perspective on the path walked, and it needs to join in attention with the forward-facing worker at the same time...I suppose that means the compiler function works that way."

